array: A data structure that stores multiple values of the same type in a single variable
we can say ,array = a list of values stored together.
An array is used when we need to store multiple values of the 
same type in one variable instead of creating many separate variables.
<br>
2. Key C# Syntax
<br>
int[] numbers = {10, 20, 30, 40};

Console.WriteLine(numbers[0]); // first element

for (int i = 0; i < numbers.Length; i++)
{
    Console.WriteLine(numbers[i]); // loop through array
}
<br>
int[] = array of integers
numbers[0] = index access (first element)
Length = size of array
